            <ArticleTitle>[The diagnostic value of enzymes in cerebrospinal fluid (author's transl)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>699-702</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The clinical value of enzyme activities in cerebrospinal fluid (CSF) should be proved by examination of GOT, GPT, LDH and CPK in blood and CSF of 115 unselected and 4 selected patients. Only the GOT showed a significant correlated increase in diffuse vascular diseases in both, serum and CSF. Discussing the literature the authors affirm, that only mechanical or functional lesion of the blood-brain-barrier will increase the enzyme activities in serum and CSF. The origin of these enzymes however is unknown till now.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
